 {"topic":"copy_stage_commit","finding":"Copied bytes and unchanged conversion provenance are checked before literal NUL-list staging. Exact stage-zero modes/IDs/raw blobs, full commit parent list, changed-path set, committed modes/IDs/raw bytes and final provenance/clean gates remain mandatory."},
 {"topic":"failure_preservation","finding":"After release and receipt-namespace admission, a create-only negative records stage, write-start state and exception without rollback. Earlier admission failures deliberately require Root to retain the original tool/job evidence."},
 {"topic":"authority_boundary","finding":"This peer does not issue the four bindings, final manifest/release, complete native-process closure or application qualification. Retained-target linkage and the exact later source/build union remain separately reviewed work."}
